/*  FUNCTION NAME:      MINOF
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the label corresponding to the smallest value in a range.*/
/*  RETURNS:            value: the label paired with the smallest value
    PARAMETERS:
        values          (Required) A 1D range of numeric values.
        labels          (Required) A 1D range of labels, same size as values.
    EXAMPLE:            =MINOF({33,6,21,12}, {"Harry","Evie","Hugh","James"}) -> Evie
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-04-13  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
MINOF = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [values],
    [labels],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        result, INDEX(labels, XMATCH(MIN(values), values)),
        result
)
);
